      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Convert::ASN1 versions before 0.37 for Perl allow CPU exhaustion via exponent-notation string in INTEGER encoding.\n\nThe encoder routes any value with abs >= 2**31 to i2osp without validating that it is an integer. A string in exponent notation such as \"1e8000\" passes that threshold. Math::BigInt expands it to an 8001-digit integer, and i2osp's per-octet conversion loop is quadratic in that size.\n\nAn attacker who controls encoded INTEGER values can exhaust CPU with a short exponent-notation string.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
